# Go API patterns

## Layout

- `api/cmd/` — binaries (`server`, `migrate`, `calibrate`)
- `api/internal/handlers/` — HTTP transport only
- `api/internal/services/` — business logic
- `api/internal/store/` — persistence
- `api/internal/models/` — domain types

## Handlers

- Parse and validate input at the boundary; return typed errors via `httputil` / `handlers/response.go`
- No SQL or Alpaca calls directly in handlers — delegate to services
- Auth: use `middleware.Auth`; workspace scope on every tenant route

## Services

- Explicit errors with context; no swallowed `err`
- Table-driven tests for math and aggregation (`*_test.go` next to source)
- Config from `internal/config` / env — not hard-coded secrets

## Database

- Migrations in `api/internal/db/migrations/` — reversible `up`/`down`
- Parameterized queries via `pgx`; never interpolate user input into SQL
